<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.50%" pitch="-2.50%">
            Jacob took one of the stones of that place and put it under his head.<break time="500ms"/>
      He lay down in that place to sleep.<break time="1000ms"/>
      There was no soft bed, no covering but the sky.<break time="500ms"/>
      The ground was hard beneath him.<break time="500ms"/>
      The stone was cold against his head.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He had no tent to set up, no fire to light, no companion to keep watch.<break time="500ms"/>
      It was just Jacob, the earth, and the night coming on around him.<break time="1800ms"/>
      Think of how small a man looks lying on open ground.<break time="500ms"/>
      The land wide in every direction.<break time="500ms"/>
      The stars appearing one by one above him.<break time="500ms"/>
      The silence of a place with no name, no marker, no significance that anyone could see.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He did not choose this place because it was holy.<break time="500ms"/>
      He stopped here because the sun had set.<break time="500ms"/>
      It was simply where the day ended.<break time="1800ms"/>
      And yet this ordinary ground, this hard bed, this nameless place would become something else entirely before the night was through.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Jacob did not know that yet.<break time="500ms"/>
      He only knew that he was tired, and that the stone held his head, and that sleep was coming.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He closed his eyes.<break time="500ms"/>
      And he slept.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
